<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Bead nexus-tko2w (RDR-108: document structure lives in the catalog manifest, never in chunk metadata).

    nexus.catalog_document_chunks gains three NULLABLE per-position labels:
        section_title TEXT, section_type TEXT, page_number INTEGER

    WHY. A T3 chunk row is content-addressed: one row per (tenant, collection, chash, model), and an
    upsert merges the metadata last-writer-wins (PgVectorRepository.mergeMetadata, jsonb concatenation).
    section_title, section_type and page_number are derived from a chunk's POSITION in one document, so
    when two documents hold the same chunk text one document's labels overwrite the other's on the shared
    row (RDR-232 research 7: ART RDR-084 position 24 carried RDR-002's title). The manifest row is already
    per (tenant, doc_id, position), so the labels belong there. The writers (CatalogRepository's single
    manifest insert), the manifest reads and chash_positions carry them; the search where-filter on these
    three keys is answered per (doc_id, position) from this table (PgVectorRepository label stage).

    NO BACKFILL. NULL is the true prior state of every existing row: the only source for a backfill is the
    shared T3 metadata, which is exactly the wrong value for a shared chunk. A re-index of a document
    rewrites its manifest and fills the columns. Readers treat NULL as "unlabelled" (a negative filter keeps
    it; a reader may fall back to the chunk row's own legacy label for such a row, see the label stage).

    ADD COLUMN only, three columns in ONE statement (no UPDATE, no ALTER ... TYPE ... USING), so there is no
    DATA EFFECT line, matching tuples-009-claimed-at.xml: scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own scope excludes
    ADD COLUMN. A nullable column with no default is a catalog-only change in PostgreSQL (no table rewrite).
    No new table, so no RLS, grant or jOOQ reflection-registration change. No index: the label filter is
    reached through the existing (tenant_id, chash) index and filtered per row.

    Placed after vectors-037-reembed-jobs.xml (the tail when this landed) and before the grants-nexus-svc.xml
    runAlways block (the established late-append convention, D0.1).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="catalog-046-1" author="nexus-tko2w">
        <comment>Adds section_title TEXT, section_type TEXT and page_number INTEGER (all NULL) to nexus.catalog_document_chunks -- per-position labels, document-scoped by the manifest's (tenant_id, doc_id, position) key. An additive ADD COLUMN only (no data mutation of any existing row), so no DATA EFFECT line applies per scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own scope. NULL is the true prior state of every existing row; a re-index fills it.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_document_chunks
    ADD COLUMN section_title TEXT NULL,
    ADD COLUMN section_type  TEXT NULL,
    ADD COLUMN page_number   INTEGER NULL;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
                ALTER TABLE nexus.catalog_document_chunks
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS section_title,
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS section_type,
                    DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS page_number;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
